JBpress instantly detects a crisis from the Internet information and judges a hoax (JBpress) - Yahoo! News
“I want to know as soon as I want to know what kind of disasters and accidents occurred!”
This has a strong need not only for news organizations such as television and newspapers, but also for social infrastructure companies and local governments.
"Spectee", a service that responds to this, was developed by Spectee, an AI-based information analysis company.
[Photo] Specialized team determines the veracity of social media information with an alert from Spectty
The first way for people to learn about disasters and accidents is starting to shift from television to social media.
Social media, such as Twitter, has become an important medium for disseminating information immediately after a disaster or an accident occurs.
However, it is difficult for human hands to constantly watch overflowing information and extract useful information from them.
Specti has a function that detects information flowing through social media such as Twitter, Instagram, and Facebook about natural disasters and accidents, analyzes its contents, and distributes it to companies that use it after determining the authenticity of the information.
It is a crisis management support service that visualizes a wide range of "crisis" events with a negative impact, such as stopping or stagnating social activities (Kenjiro Murakami, CEO).
NHK at the time of the Kumamoto earthquake in April was the first major use case of Specthai, and since then, the trend of recruitment has spread rapidly among companies.
In addition to television stations, newspapers and other news organizations, there are companies that support social infrastructure such as electricity, gas, and transportation, as well as local governments all over the country.
■ Analyzing posts to determine "crisis" types and occurrence locations
Specti distributes information by following four steps: “information collection”, “analytical and content classification”, “tightening”, and “deciding authenticity”.
User companies should specify in advance the regions (prefectures, munitions, munitions, villages, etc.) and crisis categories (disasters, accidents, etc.) in which they collect information.
Specti collects posts that fall under that designation using the APIs provided by social media.
It then analyzes and categorizes the text, images, and videos contained in the collected posts.
For example, if there is a video in which there is a fire truck, black smoke is rising from the building, and there is an orange flame coming out of the room, it is classified as a “fire”.
In addition, if it is an image of an overturned car, it is classified as a "traffic accident", and if it is an image of a road covered with water, it is classified as "road flooding".
Spekti will also estimating the location of disasters and accidents.
“We often don’t know the location from the post, so we’re contemplating it with a combination of different kinds of information,” Murakami says.
For example, if road signs and billboards are reflected in an image or video, information about the place name is extracted from it, and the location is determined by comparing it with the location name database.
