"Cold water shower" brings benefits to the body and mind (Cosmopolitan) - Yahoo! News
Suppression of inflammation such as muscle pain
A study that examined the effectiveness of hydrotherapeutherapy (hydrotherapeutic treatment using water), published in The North American Journal of Medical Sciences, found that physical and mental healing effects can be expected.
It is possible to suppress muscle pain and other inflammatory effects by being bathed in cold water after exercise.
"It is important to take a cold water shower without spending as much time as possible by exercising, according to Professor Douglas Casa, who is in charge of the Korey Stringer Institute and a professor at the University of Connecticut who studies sports medicine. After you move your body, you can quickly reduce your body's body temperature to recover from inflammation and fatigue due to exercise."
Relieves Fatigue
Exercising in high temperatures causes the heart, muscles, and the skin to require more blood flow than usual.
“When you exercise, your heart rate is higher, so your blood flow to the heart increases, which requires more energy to contract your muscles, so your muscle blood flow increases. In addition, when it comes to the skin, a lot of blood flows in order to regulate your body temperature,” says Kasa.
“By taking a cold-water shower, the temperature of the skin is lowered, which suppresses the amount of blood flow sent to the skin. Instead, blood flow is sent to internal organs such as the gastrointestinal tract, making it easier for moisture and nutrition to be taken after exercise. As a result, you can reduce the amount of fatigue you feel after exercise.”
Looking forward to the hormesis effect.
Dorozevsky also explains that being bathed in cold water is expected to activate the "hormesis effect".
The hormesis effect is the idea that it’s better to have a little bit of harmful substances and stress for the body than to have no substance or stress at all.
“Hydrogen exercise, petit fasting, and cold water showers are prime examples of hormesis benefits for health. Taking a cold water shower stimulates hormones and neurotransmitters to increase physical and physical resilience and resilience.”
