The coronavirus pandemic "became closer to the arts" Online art museum "HASARD" Mr. Konno (from Hachinohe) launched (Daily Tohoku Shimbun) - Yahoo! News
There is a museum where anyone can experience art for free whenever they want.
They range from famous painters such as Claude Monet and Gustav Klimt to unknown artists in Japan.
HASARD, an online art museum, has attracted more attention from its convenience and newness since its "opening" in April, and has attracted even more attention as a result of a new lifestyle due to the coronavirus pandemic.
"I wanted to create a service where everyone can easily enjoy art," says Shinnosuke Konno, a 26-year-old representative from Hachinohe who founded the site in Hachinohe, who founded the site, who lives in Tokyo. "I wanted to create a service where anyone can easily enjoy art."
When you visit Azar, you will be surprised by the richness of the exhibition and the beauty of the images.
As of the 24th, a total of fourteen permanent exhibitions and special exhibitions have been exhibited, and ultra-high-resolution works that convey not only the color but also the texture of the brush attract visitors.
There is no need to register as a member or entrance fee, and not only viewers but also artists who want to hold a solo exhibition do not cost anything.
It also attracts a lot of attention for its unique online presentation.
Moving the painting is one of them.
In Claude Monet's permanent exhibition "It's starting to move again", it is digitally processed so that clouds, flowers, meadows, etc. move.
"I want to make it possible for people with low interest in art to be able to enter" (Konno representative), so you can enjoy the feeling of being in a picture.
Mr. Konno and I met art when I was in elementary school.
At that time, when I visited the newly completed Aomori Prefectural Museum of Art with my family with my family, I was shocked by the power of Marc Chagall when I saw three huge paintings of "Aleko".
From the next day, the art class changed to a fun time, and even after I moved to Tokyo when I went to university, I began to visit galleries and other places.
At the same time, from various points of view, I felt that there are many people who do not have many opportunities to interact with art from various perspectives, such as not being close to the museum and holding only large exhibitions in the Tokyo metropolitan area, and it is difficult to go out due to child-rearing.
While working at an IT-related company, he spent about two months setting up a site where he could appreciate art on the Internet.
The number of users reached an average of ten thousand per month in the first ten months, and after the spread of the new coronavirus, it increased to about thirty thousand.
If you can appreciate art in a free-for-all form when anyone wants to see it.
Azar’s aim was unintentionally accepted by more and more people due to the coronavirus pandemic.
Mr. Konno emphasized that the significance of art appreciation enriches the imagination.
“When your imagination is rich, you will be able to reach out to people in need.
I hope that by becoming closer to art, we want it to become a better society.”
A simple reason why the era of quality in China has ended and the era of Japanese quality is coming (modern business) - Yahoo! News
A shift in values due to the pandemic
There are various predictions and discussions about the post-pandemic world.
In terms of business, there is a possibility that there will be a change mentioned in the July 8th article "In fact, the work of "managerial "managerial management" is beginning to disappear in Japan now ... !", the article on July 4th "In the post-coronavirus world, in the world of "post-coronavirus", the "Japanese manufacturing industry" is likely to make a big comeback ... !
[Photo] "Strength of Japan" that only the Japanese do not know the true identity of "Japan's strength" ... An unexpected reality seen in Asia
In terms of the spirit, on the spiritual side, the June 26th article "The knowledge of complete combustion to those who have become aware of the end of their lives due to the corona "Let's re-evaluate the utility of "Let's re-evaluate the utility of "God's request in a difficult time" will become the mainstream on the 10th of June.
A major flow from “Chinese quality to Japanese quality” seems to be clearly visible in our eyes as a form in which these two “materials (economy and business)” and “spirit” are combined.
For example, if a T-shirt or a digital camera is defective or defective, it is infuriating, but there is no separate article in the life of the person who bought it.
On the other hand, the sloppy quality of Chinese-made masks and ventilators, which has recently become a hot topic, "China's quality" with products that are directly linked to life and safety is fatal.
No matter how cheap it is, you can’t buy such a product.
Even if you pay a considerable price, you will be looking for "Japanese-quality" products.
Of course, this trend is not only occurring in Japan.
It is also clear that Western countries, which were in a difficult situation due to a shortage of masks and medical equipment, continued to "return" them one after another due to the "Chinese quality".
Safer and more secure than cheap.
Products such as automobiles can also cause defects to be fatal (accidental deaths).
No matter how much China, South Korea and other countries go on the offensive due to the low-selling strategy of "Let's be cheap or bad", it will not be able to compete with Japanese-made products after all, and the situation as described in the June 16th article, "Do automobile manufacturers around the world bow down to Toyota after all?" is because "Japanese quality" is strongly required for the product of automobiles.
The pandemic reminded us that many other products also need to be “safe and secure.”
In addition, safety and security is important not only in "Japanese quality in manufacturing", but also in "Japanese quality in logistics and other services".
Like the toilet paper commotion, even if the production capacity is right, the intermediate distribution may be delayed and it may not arrive.
In addition, as described in the April 17th article "Who is the real culprit of the shortage of masks! Do not forgive the fire place thieves of the Chinese Communist Party government", self-sufficiency in Japan is also an important element of "safety and security".
In the event of an emergency, it is natural for any country to prioritize their own country, and it is very important to be able to procure necessities such as masks (medical equipment) and food in your own country.
