On the 25th (sponsored by Saga Shimbun and co-sponsored by Yonezawa of Glasses) was held at Yonezawa Saga Main Store in Shimoda Town, Saga City, where experts give advice on various health-related concerns.
Akio Kinoshita, director of ophthalmology at Hiramatsu Hospital (Ogi City), explained eye diseases that are deeply related to daily life, such as dry eyes and cataracts.
The dry eye is said to be a "disease of tears", explaining that the quality of the tears is collapsing and the tears do not spread evenly on the surface of the eye.
Mr. Kinoshita said, “Con contact lens users are about four times more likely,” and urged caution, saying, “Don’t use it for a long time and don’t fall asleep while wearing it.”
It showed measures such as placing the computer screen below the height of the eyes and humidification in a room where the air conditioner worked.
We also introduced ingredients and foods that are effective for dry eyes.
"Omega-3s contained in blue fish prevents the evaporation of tears, and mucin, which is often found in natto and okra, increases the quality of tears," he said.
As for cataract surgery, there are monofocal and multi-focal intraocular lenses to be inserted in place of the crystalline lens, and I touched on the differences in the appearance.
About forty people participated in the seminar.
As a measure to prevent the spread of the new coronavirus infection, it was divided into two parts, in the morning and in the afternoon with a small number of people, and we carried out temperature measurement and disinfection before admission, as well as sufficient ventilation of the venue.
